<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-ANI buys GT Tubes for 9.5 mln stg.</title>
<headline>RTRS-ANI buys GT Tubes for 9.5 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Heavy engineer Australian National Industries Ltd (ANI) said on Tuesday it had acquired the assets of GT Tubes Ltd based in the British city of Sheffield for 9.5 million sterling.</p>
<p>ANI said GT Tubes was one of the three major producers of cold-formed hollow structural sections in Britain and produced the largest range of cold formed product.</p>
<p>It said the purchase of the 100,000 tonne per annum facility in Sheffield provided ANI's Structural Steel Group with a low cost, low risk entry into the British and European markets.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
